omx-dsp (0.34.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * the old-home grep: curve-vocabulary names omx-contract's curves file by
    what it was
  * contract-dir check: the no-floor arm removes the floor as data, with node
  * checks: the rendered vocabulary header is a separate header; the goal
    check reads a built tree
  * build: find omx-contract beside a contract-free goal; doc-check skips the
    rendered vocabulary
  * contract tests: require omx-contract 3.21.0's layout; comments stripped
    token by token
  * curve: CURVE_UNITS names its standard units, rendered as
    OMX_CURVE_UNITS_STANDARD
  * curve: red first, each curve unit word names its standard unit
    (CURVE_UNITS.standard)
  * contract tests: read omx-contract 3.21.0's render and tree (the sorting
    pass)
  * Document omx_rotary_sweep and omx_rotary_instance_sweep for the docs gate
  * ts-golden: the oracle rates are read from data/primitives/rates.json
  * ts-golden: red first, the oracle rates come from
    data/primitives/rates.json, not omx-contract
  * release: the rotary's lines in the 0.34.0 changelog
  * fx: the rotary sweep functions state their outputs as a precondition
  * fx: ROTARY_LONGEST_MS is held by the rotary resolve that makes the far end
  * test: the rotary's published sweep is held to the rotors' geometry, and a
    refused instance publishes none
  * fx: OMX_ROTARY_INSTANCE_LATENCY_FRAMES is removed; the latency is the
    face's function
  * test: the rotary instance publishes one latency figure, its function (red)
  * release: omx-dsp 0.34.0 (the sorting pass)
  * readout: READOUT_RATE_HZ is this library's data, not a domain (sorting
    pass, row V22)
  * readout: READOUT_RATE_HZ is this library's readout domain (sorting pass,
    row V22)
  * tests: READOUT_RATE_HZ is the readout domain's, this library's (red
    first, row V22)
  * rates: RT_HARD_TARGET, ORACLE_FLOOR_RATES and ORACLE_FULL_RATES are this
    library's (sorting pass, row V25)
  * tests: RT_HARD_TARGET and the ORACLE rates are this library's (red first,
    row V25)
  * catalogs: the 21 curve words travel with their translations (sorting
    pass, row V26)
  * ci: every pull request body closes an issue
  * packaging, ci: the floors rise to omx-contract 3.21.0 (rows V20
    follow-up, V26)
  * curves: CURVE_AXES and CURVE_KINDS are this library's (sorting pass, row
    V26)
  * tests: CURVE_AXES and CURVE_KINDS are this library's (red first, row V26)
  * fx: ROTARY_LONGEST_MS, the rotary sweep's far end, a kernel scalar
  * test: ROTARY_LONGEST_MS, the sweep's declared far end, is the kernel's
    longest read (red)
  * fx: the rotary publishes its sweep, shortest and longest read in frames
  * test: the rotary instance publishes its sweep, and every measured lag
    lies inside it (red)
  * fx: the rotary reports its sweep's shortest read as latency (L1 for a
    modulated delay)
  * test: the rotary instance's latency is the impulse's peak at the sweep's
    shortest phase (red)
  * tools: install-confined runs in Fedora 45
  * ci, publish: check-matrix gets the fork-guarded x86 runner
  * test: the x86 runner keeps the fork guard (red)
  * ci: the deb releases follow the release set
  * ci: make test drops the Ubuntu 24.04 include
  * tools/test: the Debian jobs take no include and no ubuntu: image outside
    check-matrix (red)
  * ci, publish: the deb jobs take their cells and runner from check-matrix
  * tools/test: a check that the Debian jobs take their cell and runner from
    check-matrix (red)

